# Hundreds of families, half a chain each holding the one before, half
# holding the chain's last, each built by a function: a table of the data
# types was once rebuilt per declaration, and a type's text held every body
# it reached. A family's identity is its content, so this is the shape
# that must stay linear. Compiled at its size and at twice it, no count of
# the compiler's work grows faster than the program.
step_limit=120
. "$IDRIS_MLIR_ROOT/harness/testutils.sh"
. "$root/harness/lib/scale.sh"
scale_relation types
